              "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. On the future null cone write $p=(\\omega,\\mathbf k)$, $\\omega=|\\mathbf k|$, $\\mathbf k\\ne0$, and use the measure $d\\nu=d^3\\mathbf k/(2\\omega)$. The fiber $p^\\perp/\\mathbb Cp$ has the positive quotient form of [[lem-qft-photon-null-quotient]]. For each proper orthochronous Lorentz transformation $\\Lambda$, the action\n$$[s(p)]\\longmapsto[\\Lambda s(\\Lambda^{-1}p)]$$\nis a unitary representation on the square-integrable quotient sections. It is strongly continuous. Under the unitary identification with $\\mathcal H_T$ given by\n$T_p[\\epsilon]:=\\boldsymbol\\epsilon-(\\mathbf k/\\omega)\\epsilon^0$\nand $u(\\mathbf k)=T_p[s(p)]/\\sqrt{2\\omega}$, as in [[lem-qft-photon-null-quotient]], the free translation representation has phase $e^{i(\\omega a^0-\\mathbf k\\cdot\\mathbf a)}$. Its bosonic Fock lift has joint spectrum the closed future cone\n$$\\overline V_+=\\{(E,\\mathbf P):E\\ge|\\mathbf P|\\},$$\nwith the vacuum at $(0,\\mathbf0)$. The energy is the nonnegative sector multiplier $\\sum_{r=1}^n|\\mathbf k_r|$ with the exact maximal square-integrability domain on each sector and square-summability over sectors. These are mathematical free-field representation statements.",
