              "quote": "Assume Countable Choice and use the Minkowski coordinates and separation condition of [[lem-qft-photon-local-field-strength]], so $\\eta(x-y,x-y)=|\\mathbf x-\\mathbf y|^2-(x^0-y^0)^2$. A spacetime region $O$ means an open subset of $\\mathbb R^4$ in its standard topology. A real antisymmetric test $h=(h^{ab})$ is supported in $O$ when each component $h^{ab}\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R)$ has support contained in $O$. Two open regions $O_1,O_2$ are spacelike separated when $\\eta(x-y,x-y)>0$ for every $x\\in O_1$ and $y\\in O_2$. Let $g_h\\in\\mathcal H_T$ be the one-particle vector for such a test from [[lem-qft-photon-local-field-strength]]. The space $\\mathcal H_T$ is separable: it is the range of the bounded projection $P_T$ on the separable space $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C^3)$. Define\n$$W_O(h)=W_{\\rm Segal}(\\sqrt2\\,g_h),$$\nwhere $W_{\\rm Segal}$ is the Weyl unitary of [[lem-qft-segal-weyl-domain]]. It is bounded and unitary, and its one-parameter group has the self-adjoint field-strength closure as generator. For every open region $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$, let $\\mathcal A(O)$ be the norm-closed unital $*$-algebra generated by $W_O(h)$ for real antisymmetric tests supported in $O$; equivalently its bounded real and imaginary parts are included as observables. If $O_1,O_2$ are spacelike separated by the stated Minkowski condition, then $\\mathcal A(O_1)$ and $\\mathcal A(O_2)$ commute.",
