              "claim": "The Segal\u2013Weyl supplier [F7] requires a separable complex Hilbert space; [F8] verifies this for $\\mathfrak h_T$, and $u_j\\in\\mathfrak h_T$ by [L1]. Let $\\lambda_j=\\Lambda2^{-j}$ for $j\\ge1$, and set $u_j=U_Eh_{\\lambda_j,\\Lambda}$ and $V_j=W(-i\\sqrt2u_j)$. The difference $u_{j+1}-u_j$ is the same current amplitude restricted to the shell $\\lambda_{j+1}<\\omega<\\lambda_j$. Applying [L1]'s cutoff norm formula to that shell gives $\\|u_{j+1}-u_j\\|^2=C\\log(\\lambda_j/\\lambda_{j+1})=C$. By [L1], $\\Psi_{\\lambda_j,\\Lambda}=V_j\\Omega$. Unitarity and the Weyl product law in [F7] give $V_j^*V_{j+1}=e^{i\\theta_j}W(-i\\sqrt2(u_{j+1}-u_j))$ for some real phase $\\theta_j$. Applying the vacuum expectation formula in [F7] yields $$|\\langle\\Psi_{\\lambda_j,\\Lambda},\\Psi_{\\lambda_{j+1},\\Lambda}\\rangle_2| =e^{-\\|u_{j+1}-u_j\\|^2/2}=e^{-C\\log2/2}<1.$$",
