              "claim": "For unit vectors $x,y$, expansion of $\\|x-\\zeta y\\|^2$ and choice of $\\zeta$ to align their inner product give $\\inf_{|\\zeta|=1}\\|x-\\zeta y\\|^2=2-2|\\langle x,y\\rangle_2|$. Step 4.3 therefore gives the fixed positive adjacent-ray distance $2(1-e^{-C\\log2/2})$ along $\\lambda_j$. A projective-ray limit would make these adjacent distances tend to zero, a contradiction. Ordinary Fock-norm convergence is the special case without phase adjustment and is also impossible. The energy from step 4.2 tends to the finite value $C\\Lambda$; nonconvergence is not caused by divergent mean energy.",
