              "reason": "Example of One-charge soft photon count example: Use the one-charge prescribed current of [[pthm-qft-example-soft-coherent-counts]] with final velocity $v=\\tfrac12$ along $\\hat{\\mathbf z}$. Choose any upper photon-energy cutoff $\\Lambda>0$ in joules and set $\\lambda=\\Lambda/\\mathrm e$, where $\\mathrm e$ is Euler's number. The angular coefficient is $$C=\\frac{\\alpha}{\\pi}(2\\log 3-2)>0.$$ The exact cutoff coherent state therefore has mean photon count $C$, vacuum probability $e^{-C}$, and mean photon energy $C\\Lambda(1-\\mathrm e^{-1})$ joules. Each halving of $\\lambda$ increases the mean count by $C\\log 2$; the mean energy remains bounded and tends to $C\\Lambda$ as $\\lambda\\downarrow0$. These are model predictions for the prepared free state. The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
