        "statement": "Fix an integer $n\\ge1$, a canonical chart with physical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$, and the corresponding dimensionless coordinates $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$. Let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be the open domain of the numerical vector $\\hat x=(\\hat q,\\hat p)$, let $\\hat H:O\\to\\mathbb R$ be the numerical energy map with physical energy $H=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat H$, and require $\\hat H$ to have continuous partial derivatives through order two. A specified open interval $J_E\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is a regular compact-shell band when $\\hat H^{-1}(K)$ is compact in $O$ for every compact $K\\subset J_E$ and $\\nabla\\hat H$ is nonzero at every point of $\\hat H^{-1}(J_E)$.\n\nFor $\\hat E\\in J_E$, the energy shell is $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}:=\\{x\\in O:\\hat H(x)=\\hat E\\}$. The graph-chart definition of the weighted shell integral is [[def-tdmath-regular-energy-shell]]: in a local graph chart $x_i=h(z,\\hat E)$, its coarea measure is $d\\mu_{\\hat E}=dA_{\\hat E}/|\\nabla\\hat H|$, with graph-area factor and gradient in the dimensionless Euclidean coordinates. Set $D(\\hat E):=\\int_{\\Sigma_{\\hat E}}d\\mu_{\\hat E}$ and admit the preparation only when $\\Sigma_{\\hat E}\\ne\\varnothing$ and $0<D(\\hat E)<\\infty$. Its normalized shell law is $\\nu_{\\hat E}(A):=D(\\hat E)^{-1}\\mu_{\\hat E}(A\\cap\\Sigma_{\\hat E})$. The current draft theorem [[thm-tdmath-regular-energy-shell-measure]] proves the coarea identity, chart independence and positive finite shell mass under its stated $C^2$, compact-regular-band hypotheses; its statement and proof are present, while its acceptance remains unresolved. Multiplying the unnormalized shell measure by a fixed positive phase-volume normalization does not change $\\nu_{\\hat E}$.",
