        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice and the canonical Gibbs-preparation assumption [[post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble]]. Restrict to its $G=H$ branch: the declared energy operator $H$ is self-adjoint, bounded below, and measured in joules; $T>0$ is in kelvins, $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$ is in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$, and $K_\\beta=e^{-\\beta H}$ has $0<Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}K_\\beta<\\infty$. Suppose also that on an open interval $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ containing $\\beta$, every compact $C\\subset J_\\beta$ admits a summable family $a_j\\ge0$ with $(1+|E_j|^2)e^{-\\gamma E_j}\\le a_j$ for all energy eigenvalues $E_j$ and $\\gamma\\in C$. For the adopted density $\\rho_\\beta=K_\\beta/Z_\\beta$, the mean and variance of $H$ are finite and\n$$-\\partial_\\beta\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H),\\qquad \\partial_\\beta^2\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Var}_{\\rho_\\beta}(H),\\qquad S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta)=k_{\\mathrm B}\\bigl(\\log Z_\\beta+\\beta\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H)\\bigr).$$\nThus $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z_\\beta=\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H)-T S_{\\mathrm{vN}}(\\rho_\\beta)$. This statement does not extend the Helmholtz interpretation to an effective generator $H-\\mu\\mathcal N$.\n\n## Facts & Assumptions\n\n**Given:** A nonzero quantum Hilbert space, a self-adjoint energy operator $H$ bounded below, a positive assigned temperature, the adopted Gibbs preparation, a finite positive trace, and the local summable moment envelope.\n\n[F1] [[post-nrqm-many-body-canonical-equilibrium-ensemble]]: for a declared $G=H$ model with self-adjoint semibounded generator and $0<\\operatorname{Tr}e^{-\\beta H}<\\infty$, the adopted preparation is $\\rho_\\beta=e^{-\\beta H}/Z_\\beta$; the postulate explicitly assumes AC and Countable Choice and does not assert equilibration.\n\n[F2] [[def-nrqm-many-body-framework-entropy-and-free-energy]] and [[def-nrqm-framework-quantities-and-units]]: in the finite-sector class, $S=k_{\\mathrm B}s$ and $\\beta=1/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)$; the general quantum model assigns energy and temperature units but does not by itself identify a trace functional with a macroscopic state function.\n\n[L1] [[thm-tdmath-general-trace-gibbs-model]] (current batch 11 draft): for a semibounded self-adjoint operator with trace-class Gibbs exponential and the stated local moment envelope, the Gibbs weight has a countable energy eigenfamily and the normalized eigenvalue law satisfies the summable canonical mean, variance, and entropy identities. Its full current proof was inspected; its draft status remains conditional.\n\n[F3] [[def-td-si-quantities]]: $k_{\\mathrm B}$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, $T$ in kelvins, and energy in joules; hence $\\beta$ is in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$ and $\\beta E_j$ is dimensionless.\n\n[A1] The full Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice are assumed at the exact strengths required by [F1] and [L1].\n\n## Proof\n\n**Given:** The $G=H$ reading of the adopted quantum Gibbs preparation, trace finiteness, and the local moment envelope.\n\n1.1 By [F1], $K_\\beta=e^{-\\beta H}$ is the declared positive Gibbs weight and $\\rho_\\beta=K_\\beta/Z_\\beta$ is the model's adopted preparation. The semiboundedness, positive finite trace, AC assumptions and moment envelope in the Statement match the hypotheses of [L1]. [F1, F3, L1, A1]\n\n2.1 Applying [L1] to this operator yields the finite mean and variance identities and the dimensionless spectral entropy identity $\\frac{S_{\\mathrm{vN}}}{k_{\\mathrm B}}=\\log Z_\\beta+\\beta\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H)$. Multiplying by $k_{\\mathrm B}$ and using $\\beta k_{\\mathrm B}=1/T$ gives $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_\\beta H)-T S_{\\mathrm{vN}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z_\\beta$. The deduction is conditional on [L1] and the adopted preparation; it asserts no dynamics. [F1, F2, F3, L1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎",
