        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let $(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ be a measure space with dimensionless reference measure, let $E:X\\to\\mathbb R\\,\\mathrm J$ be measurable, and let $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ be open. Suppose $Z(\\beta)=\\int_Xe^{-\\beta E}\\,d\\mu$ is positive and finite on $J_\\beta$, and for each compact $K\\subset J_\\beta$ there is an integrable $G_K\\ge0$ with $(1+|E|^2)e^{-\\beta E}\\le G_K$ for every $\\beta\\in K$. Under the canonical sampling assumption [[post-td-canonical-sampling]], define $p_\\beta=e^{-\\beta E}/Z$, $\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta=\\int E p_\\beta\\,d\\mu$, and $\\operatorname{Var}_\\beta(E)=\\int(E-\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta)^2p_\\beta\\,d\\mu$. Then $Z\\in C^2$, $-\\partial_\\beta\\log Z=\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta$, $\\partial_\\beta^2\\log Z=\\operatorname{Var}_\\beta(E)$, and the relative Gibbs entropy is finite with $S_\\beta=-k_{\\mathrm B}\\int p_\\beta\\log p_\\beta\\,d\\mu=k_{\\mathrm B}(\\log Z+\\beta\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta)$. Hence $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z=\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta-TS_\\beta$ for $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$.\n\n## Facts & Assumptions\n\n**Given:** A dimensionless measure space, a measurable energy, positive finite partition integrals, the canonical density, and the stated local integrable envelope.\n\n[F1] [[def-tdmath-measure-integral]]: measurable nonnegative energies and their nonnegative integrals are interpreted on the specified measure space; signed integrals require absolute integrability.\n\n[F2] [[post-td-canonical-sampling]]: with $0<Z(\\beta)<\\infty$, the density $p_\\beta=e^{-\\beta E}/Z$ is the adopted canonical preparation relative to $\\mu$.\n\n[L1] [[thm-tdmath-measurable-canonical-identities]] (current batch 11 draft): under the stated $Z$ and compact-interval domination hypotheses, $Z$ is $C^2$, the mean and variance are its log derivatives, and the relative entropy is finite with value $\\log Z+\\beta\\langle E\\rangle$. Its full current proof was inspected; its draft status remains conditional.\n\n[F3] [[def-td-si-quantities]]: $E$ and $\\langle E\\rangle$ are in joules, $T$ is in kelvins, and $k_{\\mathrm B}$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, so $\\beta$ is in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$.\n\n[A1] The reference measure is dimensionless, $Z$ is positive finite on the open interval, and $(1+|E|^2)e^{-\\beta E}$ has the local integrable envelope stated in the Statement.\n\n## Proof\n\n**Given:** The dimensionless reference measure, the measurable energy, the normalized canonical density, and the local envelope.\n\n1.1 The hypotheses in the Statement match [L1], including positive finite $Z$ and the integrable envelope on each compact parameter interval. The density in [F2] is therefore normalized and has finite first and second energy moments. [F1, F2, F3, L1, A1]\n\n2.1 Applying [L1] yields the $C^2$ partition integral, logarithmic mean and variance identities, and the finite relative entropy formula. Multiplying the dimensionless entropy by $k_{\\mathrm B}$ gives $S_\\beta=k_{\\mathrm B}(\\log Z+\\beta\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta)$; since $\\beta k_{\\mathrm B}=1/T$, rearranging gives $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=\\langle E\\rangle_\\beta-TS_\\beta=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z$. This conclusion is conditional on the draft mathematical supplier. [F2, F3, L1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎",
