te-dimensional spatial sectors.\n\nThese are distinct definitions on different domains: $S_c$ acts on an equilibrium macrostate, $S_{\\mathrm B}$ on a chosen macrocell, $S_{\\mathrm G}$ on a specified probability vector, and $S_{\\mathrm{vN}}$ on a finite-sector density operator. A numerical equality among them requires an additional, explicit identification of model, coarse-graining, preparation and applicable limit. This item supplies no such identification and adopts no canonical or microcanonical sampling rule.",
