        "id": "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Diagonal gap for a decreasing integrable interaction tail",
        "statement": "Let $d\\geq1$ and let $\\phi$ be a regular potential with a nonnegative nonincreasing envelope $\\psi:[R_0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$, where $R_0<\\infty$ and $\\int_{R_0}^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr<\\infty$. Thus $|\\phi(x)|\\leq\\psi(|x|_\\infty)$ for $|x|_\\infty\\geq R_0$. For $g>2R_0$ set\n$$\\eta(g)=g^d\\psi(g)+\\int_g^\\infty r^{d-1}\\psi(r)dr.$$\nThen $\\eta(g)\\to0$ and\n$$\\sum_{m=1}^\\infty m^{d-1}\\psi(mg)\\leq 2^{d-1}g^{-d}\\eta(g).$$\nMoreover, there is a choice $g(\\ell)>0$, for all sufficiently large real $\\ell$, such that $g(\\ell)\\to\\infty$, $g(\\ell)/\\ell\\to0$, and\n$$\\left(\\frac{\\ell}{g(\\ell)}\\right)^d\\eta(g(\\ell))\\longrightarrow0.$$\nFor every fixed finite configuration and all sufficiently large periods $L$, the noncoincident periodic-image tail $\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^d,\\ |k|_\\infty\\geq K_0}|\\phi(x-y+Lk)|$ is absolutely convergent. The tail of the cell envelope $\\psi(|j|_\\infty-1)$ over all sufficiently large integer offsets is summable. This lemma is a deterministic tail estimate; it uses no superstability or thermodynamic-limit conclusion.\n\n",
        "deps": [
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction": "mathematical-premise"
