        "statement": "Assume the superstable regular model of [[thm-tdmath-periodic-fixed-n-limit]], an interior density $N_L/L^d\\to\\rho$, and differentiability of $\\beta\\mapsto F_\\beta(\\rho)$ at $\\beta>0$. Put $e=-\\partial_\\beta F_\\beta(\\rho)$. Suppose the grand variational minimizer at a supporting activity $z>0$ is a singleton $P_*$. Let $R_{L,\\omega}$ be the periodized empirical field of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]]. There exists a specified sequence $\\delta_L\\downarrow0$ such that the uniform positional shell law\n$$Q_{\\Lambda_L}\\!\\left(\\,\\cdot\\ \\middle|\\ N=N_L,\\ \\left|H_{L,\\mathrm{per}}/L^d-e\\right|\\leq\\delta_L\\right)$$\nis eventually defined, and its empirical field converges in probability in $\\tau_L$ to $P_*$. The free and periodic exact-$N$ canonical empirical fields and the matching periodic grand-canonical empirical field converge in probability to the same limit. The energy width $2\\delta_LL^d=o(L^d)$; no arbitrary prescribed width or zero-width surface measure is asserted.\n\n",
