$Q_R\\psi\\to Q\\psi$ and $Q_RO\\psi\\to QO\\psi$ as integer $R\\to\\infty$. Then $[Q,O]\\psi=0$ on $D$. A bounded charge-changing operator satisfying $[Q,O]\\psi=qO\\psi$ for $q\\ne0$ on $D$ must therefore be the zero operator. These continuum conclusions are conditional on the displayed domain, locality, convergence and commutator-passage assumptions.\n\n",
