        "statement": "For every admitted closed process record $P\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{cl}}(s)$ of an isolated compound, assume its declared outer boundary is isolated throughout, its material constitution is fixed, its center-of-mass kinetic and separately tracked external-field potential energies have zero endpoint change, and both endpoint preparations are equilibrium macrostates. Include every named auxiliary and work device in the compound. Fix the finite constituent split $s_1,\\ldots,s_m$ used for the endpoint bookkeeping, with $m\\in\\mathbb N$, $m\\ge1$, and constitutions $c_1,\\ldots,c_m$. The split accounts for every constituent whose entropy can change; any included auxiliary not represented in it must have an explicitly model-declared zero entropy change between these endpoints. Its endpoint product is\n\n$$\\mathcal D:=D_{c_1}\\times\\cdots\\times D_{c_m},\\qquad \\mathcal F\\subseteq\\mathcal D,$$\n\nwhere $\\mathcal F$ is the model-declared feasible endpoint set for the fixed totals, retained barriers, and permitted exchanges, as in [[def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set]]. The process model supplies an endpoint association on the two formal endpoint labels $-$ and $+$:\n\n$$\\rho_P:\\{-,+\\}\\longrightarrow\\mathcal F,\\qquad \\rho_P(-)=\\mathbf x_P^-=(x_{1,P}^-,\\ldots,x_{m,P}^-),\\qquad \\rho_P(+)=\\mathbf x_P^+=(x_{1,P}^+,\\ldots,x_{m,P}^+),$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x_P^-$ and $\\mathbf x_P^+$ are respectively the declared constituent-state tuples representing the aggregate equilibrium endpoints $x_P^-$ and $x_P^+$ of $P$. Both tuples must belong to the same $\\mathcal F$. Restrict to endpoint splits admitted by [[post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy]] as a collection of independent separated macroscopic systems, so that its additive entropy rule applies. On this admitted $\\mathcal F$, define\n\n$$S_{\\mathrm{tot}}(\\mathbf x):=\\sum_{i=1}^{m}S_{c_i}(x_i)\\qquad\\left(\\mathbf x=(x_1,\\ldots,x_m)\\in\\mathcal F\\right).$$\n\nThis uses the finite