        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume [[def-tdmath-comparison-and-stability]] on compounds over a nonempty state set $X$, a strict reference pair $x_0\\preceq x_1$ with not $x_1\\preceq x_0$, and the complete ordered field $\\mathbb R$. For $x\\in X$ define\n\n$$L_x:=\\{\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R:R_\\lambda\\preceq_s e_x\\}.$$\n\nThen $L_x$ is nonempty, bounded above, and downward closed. Its supremum $S(x):=\\sup L_x$ is a real number and satisfies $R_{S(x)}\\sim_s e_x$. Stability is used to prove attainment; no continuity of states or order is assumed.",
        "strategy": "Proof strategy: direct\n\n**Given:** [A1]–[F5], with $x\\in X$ fixed.\n\n1.1 Suppose no positive integer $n$ satisfies $(n+1)e_{x_0}\\preceq ne_{x_1}+e_x$. Both sides have mass $n+1$, so CH gives $ne_{x_1}+e_x\\preceq(n+1)e_{x_0}$. Scale by $1/n$ to obtain $e_{x_1}+n^{-1}e_x\\preceq e_{x_0}+n^{-1}e_{x_0}$. Apply stability to the sequence $\\epsilon_n=1/n$, with bases $e_{x_1},e_{x_0}$ and spectators $e_x,e_{x_0}$, each of mass one. It yields $x_1\\preceq x_0$, contradicting strictness. Thus some $n$ has $(n+1)e_{x_0}\\preceq ne_{x_1}+e_x$, which by [F2] is $R_{-n}\\preceq_s e_x$; hence $-n\\in L_x$. [A1, F1, F2, F4]\n\n1.2 Suppose $L_x$ is unbounded above. For each positive integer $n$, unboundedness supplies $\\lambda\\in L_x$ with $\\lambda>n$; [F3] gives $R_n\\preceq_sR_\\lambda$, and transitivity gives $n\\in L_x$. By [F2], $R_n\\preceq_s e_x$ is the compound comparison $e_{x_0}+n e_{x_1}\\preceq e_x+n e_{x_0}$. Scaling by $1/n$ gives $e_{x_1}+n^{-1}e_{x_0}\\preceq e_{x_0}+n^{-1}e_x$. Stability with bases $e_{x_1},e_{x_0}$ and spectators $e_{x_0},e_x$ now yields $x_1\\preceq x_0$, again a contradiction. Therefore $L_x$ is bounded above. [A1, F1, F2, F3, F4]\n\n2.1 If $\\lambda\\in L_x$ and $\\mu\\le\\lambda$, [F3] gives $R_\\mu\\preceq_sR_\\lambda$; signed transitivity and $R_\\lambda\\preceq_s e_x$ imply $\\mu\\in L_x$. Thus $L_x$ is downward closed. By steps 1.1 and 1.2 it is nonempty and bounded above, so [F5] supplies the real number $s:=\\sup L_x$. [A1, F2, F3, F5, step 1.1, step 1.2]\n\n3.1 For each $n$, $s-1/n$ is not an upper bound of $L_x$, so some $\\lambda\\in L_x$ has $\\lambda>s-1/n$. Downward closure gives $s-1/n\\in L_x$. Consistency then gives $R_s+n^{-1}e_{x_0}\\preceq_s e_x+n^{-1}e_{x_1}$, because $R_{s-1/n}+n^{-1}e_{x_1}=R_s+n^{-1}e_{x_0}$. Let $K:=R_s^-$. Adding the fixed nonnegative map $K$ to both sides converts this signed comparison into the compound comparisons $R_s^++n^{-1}e_{x_0}\\preceq e_x+K+n^{-1}e_{x_1}$. Their