        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let $I$ be a specified nonempty countable microstate list with energies $E_i$ in joules, counted once, and let $J_\\beta\\subset(0,\\infty)$ be open. For $\\beta\\in J_\\beta$, define $Z(\\beta)=\\sum_i e^{-\\beta E_i}$ and, when $0<Z(\\beta)<\\infty$, $p_i(\\beta)=e^{-\\beta E_i}/Z(\\beta)$. Suppose every compact interval $K\\subset J_\\beta$ admits a summable sequence $a_i\\ge0$ with $(1+|E_i|^2)e^{-\\beta E_i}\\le a_i$ for all $i$ and $\\beta\\in K$. Then $Z$ is $C^2$, $-\\partial_\\beta\\log Z=\\bar E_\\beta$, $\\partial_\\beta^2\\log Z=\\operatorname{Var}_\\beta(E)$, and the dimensionless Gibbs entropy is finite with\n$$-\\sum_i p_i\\log p_i=\\log Z+\\beta\\bar E_\\beta.$$\nThus $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z=\\bar E_\\beta-TS_\\beta$ for $\\beta=(k_{\\mathrm B}T)^{-1}$. A lower bound on the energies alone does not supply the summable envelope or finite partition function.\n\n## Facts & Assumptions\n\n**Given:** A specified countable energy list, a positive finite canonical partition sum on $J_\\beta$, and the local summable second-moment envelope.\n\n[F1] [[def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model]]: $I$ has a specified enumeration, $Z=\\sum_i e^{-\\beta E_i}$ uses the nonnegative series convention, and $p_i$ and expectations are defined only when $0<Z<\\infty$.\n\n[F2] [[post-td-canonical-sampling]]: for this normalized countable model, $p_i=e^{-\\beta E_i}/Z$ is the adopted preparation law.\n\n[L1] [[thm-tdmath-summable-canonical-differentiation]] (current batch 11 draft): under the local envelope $(1+|E_i|^2)e^{-\\beta E_i}\\le a_i$ on each compact interval, the normalized series has the stated $C^2$, mean, variance, and entropy identities. Its full current proof was inspected; its draft status remains conditional.\n\n[F3] [[def-td-si-quantities]]: $E_i$ and $\\bar E_\\beta$ are in joules, $T$ is in kelvins, and $k_{\\mathrm B}$ is in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, so $\\beta$ is in $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$.\n\n[A1] The energy list and degeneracy convention are fixed while $\\beta$ varies; every compact interval in $J_\\beta$ has the stated summable envelope.\n\n## Proof\n\n**Given:** The countable model and its local envelope on the open interval $J_\\beta$.\n\n1.1 The assumptions in the Statement are exactly the countable model and envelope required by [L1]; the weights are counting weights, so each listed state contributes one factor $e^{-\\beta E_i}$. By [F2], their normalized law is the adopted canonical preparation, and [F3] gives the SI dimensions. [F1, F2, F3, L1, A1]\n\n2.1 Apply [L1] to this model: $Z\\in C^2$, its logarithmic derivatives give the mean and variance, and the absolutely convergent entropy sum equals $\\log Z+\\beta\\bar E_\\beta$. Multiplying the entropy identity by $k_{\\mathrm B}$ and using $\\beta k_{\\mathrm B}=1/T$ yields $F_{\\mathrm{stat}}=\\bar E_\\beta-TS_\\beta=-k_{\\mathrm B}T\\log Z$. The claim remains conditional on the draft supplier's proof and the envelope. [F2, F3, L1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎",
