        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Fix an integer $n\\ge1$ and an open phase-coordinate domain $O_{\\rm phys}\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ with physical canonical coordinates $q_i$ in metres and $p_i$ in $\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$. The canonical symplectic form on this chart is $\\omega_{\\rm phys}=\\sum_{i=1}^n dq_i\\wedge dp_i$. Let $\\hat q_i=q_i/(1\\,\\mathrm m)$ and $\\hat p_i=p_i/(1\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}})$, and let $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{2n}$ be the open image of the chart in these dimensionless coordinates. The corresponding dimensionless canonical form is $\\hat\\omega=\\sum_{i=1}^n d\\hat q_i\\wedge d\\hat p_i$, so $\\omega_{\\rm phys}=(1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,s})\\hat\\omega$.\n\nLet $\\hat H:O\\to\\mathbb R$ be a numerical energy function with continuous partial derivatives through order two, and let $H_{\\rm phys}:O_{\\rm phys}\\to\\mathbb R\\,\\mathrm J$ be $H_{\\rm phys}(q,p)=(1\\,\\mathrm J)\\hat H(\\hat q,\\hat p)$. Where defined, its physical Hamiltonian vector field $X_{H_{\\rm phys}}$ is determined by $\\iota_{X_{H_{\\rm phys}}}\\omega_{\\rm phys}=dH_{\\rm phys}$. For each elapsed time $t$ in its domain, the physical flow map is a function $\\phi_t:D_t\\to O_{\\rm phys}$, where $D_t\\subseteq O_{\\rm phys}$ is the set of initial data whose trajectories exist through time $t$, and it satisfies $d\\phi_t/dt=X_{H_{\\rm phys}}\\circ\\phi_t$. Equivalently, in the dimensionless chart, the flow map $\\hat\\phi_{\\hat t}:\\hat D_{\\hat t}\\to O$ is generated by $X_{\\hat H}$ satisfying $\\iota_{X_{\\hat H}}\\hat\\omega=d\\hat H$, at dimensionless time $\\hat t=t/(1\\,\\mathrm s)$; here $\\hat D_{\\hat t}$ is the set of initial coordinates whose trajectories exist through $\\hat t$. These definitions specify the flow maps when they exist but impose no global-existence or completeness hypothesis on the shell preparation.\n\nA specified open interval $J_E\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ is a regular compact-shell band when $\\hat 