        "statement": "For a bounded set $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ and $R>0$, define its two-sided boundary layer\n$$\\partial_R\\Omega=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\operatorname{dist}(x,\\partial\\Omega)\\leq R\\},$$\nwhere distance is Euclidean distance and $|\\cdot|$ denotes $d$-dimensional Lebesgue measure. A van Hove sequence is a sequence of bounded Lebesgue measurable sets $(\\Omega_k)_{k\\geq1}$ with $0<|\\Omega_k|<\\infty$, $|\\Omega_k|\\to\\infty$, and\n$$\\frac{|\\partial_R\\Omega_k|}{|\\Omega_k|}\\longrightarrow0\\qquad\\text{for every fixed }R>0.$$\nThe condition controls both inner and outer boundary neighborhoods. It does not impose connectedness, a bounded aspect ratio, smooth boundaries, or a periodic identification.\n",
