        "title": "Interacting density-interval and upper-energy event limit",
        "statement": "Assume the superstable regular model and Poisson conventions of [[thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure]]. Let $D\\subset[0,\\infty)$ be an interval of positive length, let $\\nu$ be the supremum of finite-entropy, finite-energy attainable densities, and set $e_0(\\rho)=\\inf\\{\\Phi(P):\\rho(P)=\\rho,\\ I(P)<\\infty\\}$. If $\\inf D<\\nu$ and $e>\\inf_{\\rho\\in D}e_0(\\rho)$, define\n$$A_L=\\{N_{\\Lambda_L}/L^d\\in D,\\ H_{L,\\mathrm{per}}/L^d\\leq e\\}.$$\nThen $A_L$ has positive Poisson probability for all sufficiently large $L$, and\n$$\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Q_{\\Lambda_L}(A_L) =-\\min\\{I(P):\\rho(P)\\in\\overline D,\\ \\Phi(P)\\leq e\\}.$$\nLet $R_{L,\\omega}$ be the periodized empirical field of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]]. There are $\\beta\\geq0$ and $z>0$ such that the empirical fields under the conditional law $Q_{\\Lambda_L}(\\cdot\\mid A_L)$ and the matching periodic grand-canonical law concentrate in every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood of the common minimizer set of $I+\\beta\\Phi-\\rho\\log z$ when $\\beta>0$. At $\\beta=0$, retain the forbidden-pair set $B=\\{x:\\phi(x)=+\\infty\\}$ and use $I-\\rho\\log z$ on the hard-admissible stationary class $\\mathcal K_B$, with grand weight $z^N\\mathbf1_{\\rm admissible}$; no value is assigned to $0\\cdot(+\\infty)$. If this minimizer is unique, both empirical fields converge to it in probability in $\\tau_L$. These are empirical-field conclusions. The periodically continued conditional and grand laws also converge in $\\tau_L$ under the same uniqueness assumption, for all measurable local observables of at-most-linear count growth. The energy constraint is an upper event and $D$ is nondegenerate; this does not assert exact $N$, a shrinking shell, or a singular energy surface.",
