        "title": "Complete integrals and covariant versus time Hamilton-Jacobi",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/HJ supplier chain and let $n\\ge1$. Let $U_H\\subset\\mathbb R\\times T^*\\mathbb R^n$ be open and $H\\in C^\\infty(U_H,\\mathbb R)$. Let $D_S\\subset\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^n_q\\times\\mathbb R^n_\\alpha$ be open and $S\\in C^3(D_S,\\mathbb R)$, with $S_t+H(t,q,S_q)=0$ wherever $(t,q,\\alpha)\\in D_S$ and $(t,q,S_q(t,q,\\alpha))\\in U_H$. If the mixed matrix $S_{q\\alpha}$ is invertible at $(t,q,\\alpha)$, then after restricting neighborhoods the equations $p_i=S_{q^i}$, $\\beta^i=S_{\\alpha_i}$ define a local $C^2$ diffeomorphism $F_t:(q,p)\\mapsto(\\beta,\\alpha)$ at each fixed $t$. Equip the old chart $(q,p)$ with $\\omega_{\\rm old}=\\sum_i dq^i\\wedge dp_i$ and the target chart, whose position coordinates are $\\beta^i$ and momentum coordinates are $\\alpha_i$, with $\\omega_{\\rm new}=\\sum_i d\\beta^i\\wedge d\\alpha_i$. Then $F_t^*\\omega_{\\rm new}=\\omega_{\\rm old}$, so this is a local canonical transformation in the stated convention, and $\\beta$ is constant along the Hamilton characteristics $\\dot q=H_p$, $\\dot p=-H_q$. Such a family is a complete integral only on that nonsingular local domain. In the physical interpretation, $q^i,\\beta^i$ have units m, $p_i,\\alpha_i$ have units kg m/s, $t$ has units s, and $S$ has units J s. In a temporal spacetime chart satisfying H9, the covariant future-shell equation $g^{ab}S_aS_b+m^2c^2=0$ reduces to the time Hamilton–Jacobi equation with $p_0=S_t/c=-H/c$; for $m=0$ require a nonzero future null covector. $S$ is an action, not a dimensionless phase.\n\nFor the relativistic shell equation, $m$ is measured in kilograms and $c$ in metres per second.",
