        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Conditional particle trajectories from Hamilton-Jacobi characteristics",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/H7/H9 supplier chain. Adopt the massive free action or separate massless shell action in [[post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action]] and [[post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action]]. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open time interval, $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ an open spatial chart domain, and $(N,\\beta,h)$ smooth temporal-chart data with $N>0$ and $h_{ij}$ positive definite as in [[def-rpm-h-temporal-chart-data]]. Take $m\\ge0$ in kg and $c>0$ in m/s. On the future shell define $\\kappa(t,q,p)=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+h^{ij}(t,q)p_ip_j}$ and the positive-root reduced Hamiltonian $H(t,q,p)=c\\bigl(N\\kappa-\\beta^ip_i\\bigr)$ from [[thm-rpm-h-temporal-shell-reduction]]; its domain is $U=I\\times T^*\\Omega$ for $m>0$, and the open subset with $p\\ne0$ for $m=0$. Here $t$ is measured in seconds, $q$ in metres, $p$ in kg m/s, $H$ in joules, and $S$ in joule-seconds. Let $D\\subseteq I\\times\\Omega$ be open and let $S\\in C^2(D,\\mathbb R)$ (all partial derivatives through order two are continuous) satisfy $S_t+H(t,q,S_q)=0$ wherever $(t,q,S_q)\\in U$. If $S$ is the smooth local solution supplied by [[thm-rpm-h-local-hamilton-jacobi]] from an initial exact-graph point in $U$, and $J=[t_1,t_2]\\subset I$ with $t_1<t_2$ is an interval on which its characteristic projection remains invertible, let $q:J\\to\\Omega$ be a $C^1$ characteristic with $\\dot q=H_p(t,q,S_q)$. Then $p(t):=S_q(t,q(t))$ satisfies $\\dot p=-H_q$, so $(q,p)$ obey Hamilton's equations. The smooth ODE makes this characteristic smooth; by [[thm-rpm-h-temporal-shell-reduction]] these reduced equations are exactly the equations of the future-shell first-order system of [[thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics]]. Under the matching adopted model postulate, this curve is a trajectory of the massive or separate massless model. The conclusion holds only on the chart and local solution interval; it does not continue through a caustic or assert a global HJ solution. It is a conditional mathematical prediction, not a reported observation.\n\nThe characteristic graph is restricted to points with $(t,q,S_q(t,q))\\in U$. The action $S$ is measured in joule-seconds.",
