        "title": "Two scalar shell potentials fail first-class closure generically",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the cotangent/constraint supplier. Use the product cotangent domain $\\mathcal P=T^*(\\mathbb R^4\\times\\mathbb R^4)$ with coordinates $(x_i^a,p_{ia})$ for $i=1,2$, Minkowski metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, canonical form $\\omega=\\sum_{i=1}^2\\sum_{a=0}^3dx_i^a\\wedge dp_{ia}$, and induced bracket $\\{F,G\\}=\\sum_{i=1}^2\\sum_{a=0}^3(F_{x_i^a}G_{p_{ia}}-F_{p_{ia}}G_{x_i^a})$. Take $x_i^a$ in metres, $p_{ia}$ in kg m/s, $P_i^a:=\\eta^{ab}p_{ib}$, $p_i^2:=\\eta^{ab}p_{ia}p_{ib}$, $r^a:=x_1^a-x_2^a$, and $r^2:=\\eta_{ab}r^ar^b$. Use constraints\n\n$$C_1=\\tfrac12(p_1^2+m_1^2c^2)+V(r^2),\\qquad C_2=\\tfrac12(p_2^2+m_2^2c^2)+V(r^2).$$\n\nHere $m_i>0$ in kg, $c>0$ in m/s, and $V:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ is smooth with units of momentum squared. Their canonical bracket is\n\n$$\\{C_1,C_2\\}=-2V'(r^2)\\,r\\cdot(P_1+P_2).$$\n\nFor $V(z)=\\lambda z$, with $\\lambda>0$ in momentum squared per square metre, this bracket is nonzero at explicit points on the joint surface $C_1=C_2=0$ where $dC_1,dC_2$ are independent. Thus, by [[def-rpm-h-first-class-constraint-family]], the pair fails first-class closure on the local regular surface around each such point, and arbitrary independent multipliers need not preserve both constraints there. Additional consistency conditions are required; no universal obstruction for all interacting relativistic models is claimed.",
