s are $M_{\\!p}=c^2m_{\\mathrm{geo}}/G$, $Q_e=\\sqrt{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0c^4/G}\\,q_{\\mathrm{geo}}$, $J_{\\mathrm{ang}}=M_{\\!p}c\\,a_{\\mathrm{geo}}$, and $\\Phi_B=4\\pi p_{\\mathrm{geo}}/\\alpha$.\n\nThe mass, charge, angular momentum and flux are inputs to this dictionary; their primitive or derived status in any physical model is framework-specific. No field equation, Maxwell postulate, matter law, or empirical value is part of this definition.",
