        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, the hypothesis of [[thm-qft-algebraic-gns-domain]]. Let $G$ be a topological group with identity $e$. Let $A$ be a unital complex star algebra with positive normalized state $\\omega$, and let $\\alpha:G\\to\\operatorname{Aut}^*(A)$ be a group action: each $\\alpha_g$ is a bijective complex-linear map preserving product, unit and involution, with $\\alpha_e=\\mathrm{id}$ and $\\alpha_g\\alpha_h=\\alpha_{gh}$. Suppose $\\omega(\\alpha_g(a))=\\omega(a)$ for all $g\\in G$ and $a\\in A$. Also suppose that, for every $a,b\\in A$, the coefficient function $g\\mapsto\\omega(b^*\\alpha_g(a))$ is continuous at $e$.\n\nUse the GNS representation from [[thm-qft-algebraic-gns-domain]], with common dense domain $\\mathcal D_\\omega$ and cyclic vector $\\Omega_\\omega$. Then $U_g[a]:=[\\alpha_g(a)]$ extends to a strongly continuous unitary representation $U:G\\to\\mathcal U(H_\\omega)$, fixes $\\Omega_\\omega$, and satisfies\n\n$$U_g\\pi_\\omega(a)U_g^{-1}|_{\\mathcal D_\\omega}=\\pi_\\omega(\\alpha_g(a))\\qquad(a\\in A,g\\in G).$$\n\nHere strongly continuous means that $g\\mapsto U_g\\xi$ is norm-continuous for every $\\xi\\in H_\\omega$. No differentiability, generator domain or spectral theorem follows from these hypotheses alone.",
